From: XOS contributors
Subject: [PATCH] configure: scope XOS modules to what the runtime provides

XOS has no fork/exec, select, pty, dlopen or system zoneinfo database, and
newlib does not implement lstat, pause, or the XSI timezone names. Keep those
modules and code paths out of the static bootstrap instead of linking against
absent symbols. Static modules are the only build type XOS can load. Link every
archive in one group: module archives follow LIBS, so libc and libgcc must be
revisited after they are seen. The target supplies secure random bytes and
POSIX TZ parsing; time.sleep() advances by spinning on monotonic PIT ticks.
--- base1/configure	2026-10-25 12:33:49
+++ mod/configure	2026-10-25 12:33:36
